  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Rubies and sapphires are the same stone.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#c8143c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Both are corundum, which is aluminum oxide.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Corundum",
        "sub": "Aluminum oxide"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A trace of chromium, about 1% or less,",
      "say": "A trace of chromium, about one percent or less,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#ef9ab4",
        "openAt": 0.1,
        "label": "A trace of chromium"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "turns it red, and more chromium makes the red stronger.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cut",
        "phase": "result",
        "pieces": [
          {
            "shape": "oval",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#ef9ab4"
          },
          {
            "shape": "oval",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#dc4a74"
          },
          {
            "shape": "oval",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#c8143c"
          },
          {
            "shape": "oval",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#8a0a24"
          }
        ],
        "note": "More chromium"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Iron and titanium turn it blue instead, and that's a sapphire.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#1f4fb0",
        "openAt": 0.1,
        "label": "Iron and titanium"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Red corundum is called ruby, and every other color is sapphire.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cut",
        "phase": "result",
        "pieces": [
          {
            "shape": "oval",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#c8143c"
          },
          {
            "shape": "cushion",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#1f4fb0"
          },
          {
            "shape": "pear",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#e8b828"
          },
          {
            "shape": "round",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#ef9ab4"
          },
          {
            "shape": "emerald",
            "carats": 10,
            "tone": "#2e9e6a"
          }
        ],
        "note": "All corundum"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Labs still argue over where pink ends and ruby begins.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "study",
        "name": "Pink or ruby",
        "role": "Still argued",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "suit",
            "outfitColor": "#2a2f3d",
            "hair": "short",
            "hairColor": "#3a2c22",
            "skin": "#e2b08a",
            "glasses": "loupe",
            "prop": "gem",
            "propTone": "#d84a72",
            "expression": "focused"
          },
          {
            "outfit": "dress",
            "outfitColor": "#3a2f4a",
            "hair": "long",
            "hairColor": "#2a1d16",
            "skin": "#c98e6a",
            "glasses": "round",
            "prop": "magnifier",
            "expression": "worried"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Chromium also makes rubies glow red under ultraviolet light.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "oval",
        "tone": "#c8143c",
        "openAt": 0.1,
        "light": "#9b6bff",
        "halo": "#ff2a4a",
        "label": "Under UV light"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Burmese rubies have little iron, so they glow even in sunlight.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "mine",
        "place": "Burma",
        "tone": "#c8143c",
        "zoomAt": 0.2
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In 2015 the Burmese Sunrise Ruby sold for about $30 million.",
      "say": "In twenty fifteen the Burmese Sunrise Ruby sold for about thirty million dollars.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "ring",
        "shape": "cushion",
        "tone": "#c8143c",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Sunrise Ruby"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It's still the auction record for a ruby, per carat.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "$1.18 million",
        "sub": "Per carat, a ruby record"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "Rubies and sapphires are the same mineral. A trace of chromium is all that makes a ruby red, and it can make one glow in sunlight.",
